  %article
    #team-bios
      .bio
        %h3 Arun Thampi (@iamclovin)
        %p
          Arun always had a fascination for building things, right from childhood when he was a keen assistant to his dad who was always repairing, soldering or fixing stuff around the house. He received a scholarship from the Singapore Government to study Electrical Engineering at the National University of Singapore. During his time there, he was part of a team which pushed the envelope of a requisite electronics project by building a cellphone-operated car, when the rest of the cohort was building RF-transmittor based cars. He graduated with a Master's Degree in Technological Design and went on to become one of the first employees at Wego.com - which is now one of Asia's biggest travel websites. After spending three years learning the ropes, he set out on his own entrepreneurial journey in April 2010 and is now leading the engineering efforts at Anideo.
      .bio
        %h3 Peter Jihoon Kim  (@raingrove)
        %p
          Peter is an extraordinary human being in every regard. His history is still being written.

      .bio
        %h3 AJ Solimine
        %p
          AJ started programming during his high school math classes where he would program games on his TI-83 calculator to pass time.
        %p
          As an undergraduate at Harvard University, he took a part-time job as a researcher at the Center for Design Informatics, a human computer interaction laboratory at the Harvard Design School. He fell in love with User Experience and Interface Design and began auditing Computer Science courses during his final year at Harvard. He worked as a consultant his first year out of school before co-founding a Healthcare startup focused on developing a knowledge base for Rare Disease patients. He founded Anideo, the company behind Vidyou in 2009 with Eduardo Saverin upon moving to Singapore and leads product development and design. AJ graduated from Harvard University with a degree in Economics in 2005.


